Add the opt-in --warn-unchecked-termination option. Under it, `dafny verify` (and `dafny resolve`) warns about each trait with `{:termination false}` and each class or trait with `@AssumeCrossModuleTermination`, whose dispatched calls are not checked for termination and which before only `dafny audit` reported. The warning works as the one for an `assume` statement without `{:axiom}`: it fails the command unless `--allow-warnings` is given, and `{:axiom}` on the declaration, or `--allow-axioms`, suppresses it. It stays under `--modular-termination` (https://github.com/erniecohen/dafny/issues/211).
